probe-models-after-weekly-quota-reset

Lane: backend

FlatPatch: probe-models-after-weekly-quota-reset

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Activate model quota windows after an observed main primary weekly quota reset for the approved personal ChatGPT plans.

Requires: none

Provides: Observe real account rate-limit snapshots without replacing their request-response behavior, bind reset transitions and scheduled verification to the current account revision, and run bounded health-check turns through the native ThreadManager ephemeral lifecycle across eligible available models once per verified reset.

Boundary: Only the codex primary weekly window and Plus, Pro and ProLite accounts qualify; account changes cancel probes, catalog and OpenAI provider selection remain native, and isolated probes have no tools, execution environments, persisted conversations or rollouts. Existing model and batch deadlines, concurrency and output limits remain bounded. Native managed startup owns cancellation, shutdown and deregistration. Response observation and persistence remain with track-model-responses-by-attempt, without a TUI dependency.

Verification: Focused app-server tests cover account eligibility, primary weekly windows, identity-bound reset deduplication, native ephemeral turn completion and failure, tool and instruction isolation, cancellation cleanup, absent persisted history and the output limit.


